      "node_id": "kg_doc_7",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Barnens brevlåda (\"\"The Children's Letterbox\"\") was a Swedish children's radio programme, led by Sven Jerring. It aired totally 1 785 times, between 11 September 1925 and 1972, making it the longest-lasting Swedish radio programme of that time. The record was broken on 14 November 1999 by the programme \"Smoke Rings\".",
